#: skills/workflows/kg-to-portal.bpmn:113
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "EDITORIAL, and it is stage 1 rather than a filter bolted to the exporter. kg-export produces the WHOLE graph because inspection wants the whole graph; a portal wants what its readers may see. Running the second as the first is how a QA verdict, a bean's blocking note or an unpublished draft reaches a public cache. Decided once, here, rather than at each consumer."
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/kg-to-portal.bpmn:48
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "folio-assistant — KG to public portal. Six stages: select, serialize, package, sign, distribute, verify. Three decisions belong to the DEPLOYMENT and are drawn as gateways rather than as steps — the ingestion transport, the versioned store, and the signing scheme. A pipeline that picks one of those is asserting a decision nobody made. A CDN is a LAYER, not a publication host. PUBLICATION_HOSTS answers \"what serves the rendering\"; a cache answers \"what stands between the server and the reader\", and the canonical URL stays the origin's either way."
msgstr ""

